# ⚠️ THIS PACKAGE HAS MOVED

> ## `EulerApiSdk` is **deprecated** and no longer maintained.
>
> ## 👉 Use **[`tiktok-api-sdk`](https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-api-sdk/)** or **[`tiktok-live-api-sdk`](https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-live-api-sdk/)** instead.

`EulerApiSdk` is now two packages. Pick the one that fits:

| You want | Install | Import as |
|---|---|---|
| Everything: TikTok users, videos, OAuth, signing, captchas and the full TikTok LIVE API | [`tiktok-api-sdk`](https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-api-sdk/) | `TikTokApiSdk` |
| TikTok LIVE only | [`tiktok-live-api-sdk`](https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-live-api-sdk/) | `TikTokLiveApiSdk` |

`tiktok-api-sdk` contains everything `EulerApiSdk` did, so it is the drop-in replacement.

## Migrating

Uninstall `EulerApiSdk` first, then install the new package:

```bash
pip uninstall EulerApiSdk
pip install tiktok-api-sdk
```

Your existing code keeps running. Both new packages still answer to `import EulerApiSdk`, with a `DeprecationWarning`, so migrating is a package name change. Switch the imports when convenient:

```python
# before
from EulerApiSdk import AuthenticatedClient
from EulerApiSdk.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic

# after
from TikTokApiSdk import AuthenticatedClient
from TikTokApiSdk.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic
```

Uninstalling first matters: the new packages provide the old `EulerApiSdk` import name from the same folder this package installs into, and pip does not notice two packages sharing a folder.

All future updates, bug fixes and new API coverage ship under the new names:

### 📦 https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-api-sdk/

### 📦 https://pypi.org/project/tiktok-live-api-sdk/

